{
  "box": "ad slot (src/pages/tool/*.astro) sits below content that shrinks on tap — does the slot rise into the point the finger just touched, within a human double-tap window?",
  "method": "Real CDP touch (Input.dispatchTouchEvent) via scripts/driver.mjs against a built dist/ served locally. Per page, per shrink-handler control: grid-scan the control's box, record each tap point, compare the ad slot's bounding rect before the tap and after the DOM settles. Widths 320px and 390px. Detector calibrated red by construction (see 02).",
  "capturedAtCommit": "dc55dd7",
  "capturedAtCommitNote": "tree was DIRTY at capture. Uncommitted at the time: .github/workflows/ci.yml, docs/verification/evidence/adslot/, scripts/ad-slot-grid-probe.mjs, scripts/crawl-check-gamenav.mjs, scripts/thai-comments.mjs, src/games/_arm-gate.ts, src/games/short-stick.test.mjs, src/games/short-stick.ts, src/games/timebomb.test.mjs, src/games/timebomb.ts. None of these touch src/pages/tool/*.astro or src/layouts/, which are the files this walk measures.",
  "verdict": "PROVEN",
  "noTapPointInsidePostTapAdRect": true,
  "detectorProvenAbleToGoRed": true,
  "scopeNotCovered": [
    "The slot is an empty <div style='min-height:250px'>, not a live AdSense iframe. The result generalises to IN-FLOW manual ad units only: for those, the slot's TOP edge is set by the height of the content above it, not by the ad's own height, so a taller unit extends downward and the measured clearance holds. It does NOT generalise to anchor or vignette formats, which are position:fixed and are not laid out by the content above them at all — those are unmeasured.",
    "wheel.astro under DEFAULT motion is N/A, not tested: its list shrink fires ~1200ms after the tap, outside any human double-tap window. It was measured under --force-prefers-reduced-motion, where the shrink is synchronous and therefore the worst case.",
    "draw.astro and wheel.astro needed long synthetic names to produce a non-zero shrink at all; short default names (เอ/บี) flex-wrap several chips per row and shrink by 0px.",
    "number.astro has no shrink handler to test — verified by reading the file, measured for parity only.",
    "UNFILED HAZARD, different class: wheel.astro's list shrink fires ~1200ms after the tap under default motion. That is outside any double-tap window, which is why this walk calls it N/A — but a 1200ms-delayed layout shift above a live ad is a CLS misclick risk for a DELIBERATE tap. This walk does not measure that and no issue tracks it."
  ],
